<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><documents xmlns:xsi = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation = "HDocumentSchema.xsd"><document type = "H"><pnldref>H2280</pnldref><english><title>Threat to damage / destroy property</title><additionalkeywords><additionalkeyword>THREATEN</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>THREATENED</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>THREATENING</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DESTROYED</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DESTROYING</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DESTRUCTION</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DAMAGED</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>DAMAGING</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>LAWFUL EXCUSE</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>BELONGING</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>BELONG</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>INTENT</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>INTENDING</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>INTENTION</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>FEAR</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>2</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>4</additionalkeyword><additionalkeyword>CRIMINAL DAMAGE ACT 1971</additionalkeyword></additionalkeywords><standardoffencewording>On **(..SPECIFY DATE..) at **(..SPECIFY TOWNSHIP..), without lawful excuse, threatened **(..SPECIFY PERSON..) that **(..SPECIFY THREAT TO PROPERTY..) belonging to&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;(A)_[him,]_&lt;br /&gt;(B)_[her,]_&lt;br /&gt;(C)_[**(..SPECIFY OTHER PERSON..),]_&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;intending that &lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;(D)_[he]_&lt;br /&gt;(E)_[she]_&lt;br /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;would fear that the threat would be carried out</standardoffencewording><legislation>Contrary to sections 2(a) and 4 of the Criminal Damage Act 1971.</legislation><pointstoprove>date and location&lt;br /&gt;without lawful excuse threatened property of a person&lt;br /&gt;intending a person would fear that the threat would be carried out</pointstoprove><investigatoractions><investigatoraction><code>IA1</code><description>Fingerprint and photograph</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA2</code><description>DNA Samples: If crime scene stain present - take evidential sample If no crime scene stain and DNA not confirmed on PNC - take Criminal Justice sample. If DNA confirmed on PNC - CJ sample not required</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA27</code><description>Confirm proposed charge is appropriately authorised (Police or CPS)</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA28</code><description>Ensure compliance with investigator's obligations re disclosure</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA29</code><description>Consider if case suitable for referral to Financial Investigation Unit and CPS for asset recovery eg confiscation order</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA3</code><description>Audio record interview unless exempt</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA4</code><description>PNC recordable</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA5</code><description>Submit a crime report</description></investigatoraction><investigatoraction><code>IA6</code><description>Offences brought to justice scheme</description></investigatoraction></investigatoractions><policeandcpschargingresponsibilities>D27968</policeandcpschargingresponsibilities><notes>The threat may be made to the owner of property or to a third person but a threat to destroy or damage a person's own property does not constitute an offence under this section. However - see H2278 where the threat is to destroy or damage a person's own property likely to endanger life.</notes></english><indictment><indictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></indictmentindicator><structuredindictmentindicator><code>N</code><description>No</description></structuredindictmentindicator></indictment><other><powersofarrest>Arrest without warrant</powersofarrest><modeoftrial><code